"OverallSummary": "Signet Securities violated the Care Obligation under Regulation Best Interest by failing to conduct reasonable due diligence on private placement offerings that it recommended to retail investors. From June 30, 2020, to the present, the firm recommended and sold $140 million worth of securities across 13 Regulation D private placement offerings to accredited retail investors. All of these offerings were issued by affiliates of a commercial real estate investment company referred to as 'Company A.' The firm's due diligence was inadequate because: (1) it relied solely on documents provided by Company A without independent verification, (2) it failed to independently verify material representations and claims as required under FINRA Regulatory Notice 10-22, and (3) it did not maintain documentation of its due diligence process. The firm also failed to properly supervise outside business activities of registered representatives who were simultaneously employed by a Company A affiliate, creating potential conflicts of interest. Additionally, the firm failed to deliver Form CRS to 282 retail customers between June 30, 2020, and April 14, 2022, and continued to fail to deliver Form CRS to existing customers after that date. For these violations, Signet Securities was censured, fined $100,000, and required to implement remedial measures. The case does not specify individual customer losses or the exact number of retail investors affected by these violations."
